posts.body:
In base rpg maker mv I think you can just remove the animation stuff from the stateicon methods and always have it show the first index (but I didn't check this extensively). I added a conditional for it to only use the updateFrame if the icon changed (like there's a new one with higher priority, because I think it sorts the battler states when new states are added). Though depending on what other Yanfly plugins you're using, they have probably modified that stuff, but it seemed to work with some of them on when I quickly tested it.
Then you can use Olivia's State Tooltips plugin to show the rest.
Sprite_StateIcon.prototype.update = function() {
Sprite.prototype.update.call(this);
this._animationCount++;
const currentIconIndex = this._iconIndex;
if (this._animationCount >= this.animationWait()) {
this.updateIcon();
if (currentIconIndex !== this._iconIndex) {
this.updateFrame();
}
this._animationCount = 0;
}
};
Sprite_StateIcon.prototype.updateIcon = function() {
var icons = [];
if (this._battler && this._battler.isAlive()) {
icons = this._battler.allIcons();
}
if (icons.length > 0) {
this._iconIndex = icons[0];
} else {
this._iconIndex = 0;
}
};
